      {
         "id": "c",
         "prompt": "Find the value of \\( \\dfrac{d^{2}y}{dx^{2}} \\) for the curve \\( C \\) at the point \\( (1, 2) \\). Show the work that leads to your answer.",
         "setup_required": false,
         "answer_latex": "\\frac{12}{125}",
         "worked_solution": [
            {
               "text": "Slope at (1, 2) from part (b).",
               "latex": "\\frac{dy}{dx}\\Big|_{(1,2)} = -\\frac{2}{1 + 4} = -\\frac{2}{5}"
            },
            {
               "text": "Differentiate y + x dy/dx + 2y dy/dx = 0 again: the product rule on x dy/dx and on 2y dy/dx, and the chain rule on 2y.",
               "latex": "2\\frac{dy}{dx} + x\\frac{d^{2}y}{dx^{2}} + 2\\left(\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right)^{2} + 2y\\frac{d^{2}y}{dx^{2}} = 0"
            },
            {
               "text": "Substitute x = 1, y = 2 and dy/dx = -2/5, then solve.",
               "latex": "2\\left(-\\frac{2}{5}\\right) + \\frac{d^{2}y}{dx^{2}} + 2 \\cdot \\frac{4}{25} + 4\\frac{d^{2}y}{dx^{2}} = 0"
            },
            {
               "text": "Solve for the second derivative.",
               "latex": "\\frac{d^{2}y}{dx^{2}}\\Big|_{(1,2)} = \\frac{12}{125}"
            }
         ],
